    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe application now rejects a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a **400 Bad Request**.\n\n**Changes in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a `validateRegistrationDate(...)` call in `addOwner` right after email normalization and **before** the null-defaulting logic \u2014 so it only validates a client-supplied date, not the server-defaulted one:\n   ```java\n   validateRegistrationDate(owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\n2. Added the helper method, which reuses the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (already mapped to a 400 whose `errors` array names the offending field, consistent with `postcode`/`email` validation):\n   ```java\n   private void validateRegistrationDate(LocalDate registrationDate) {\n       if (registrationDate != null && registrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n           throw new InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"registrationDate\"));\n       }\n   }\n   ```\n\nA `null` (omitted) date is still accepted and defaults to the server date; only a supplied future date is rejected. The `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
